  "details": "- CVE-2026-63718: fix mod_proxy_uwsgi response smuggling via hop-by-hop\n  headers from the backend\n- CVE-2026-73636: fix mod_auth_digest one-time nonce replay\n- CVE-2026-73637: fix mod_auth_digest use-after-free on concurrent requests\n- CVE-2026-48005: fix mod_auth_digest forced re-authentication via forged\n  Authorization headers with AuthDigestNcCheck\n- mod_auth_digest: configs using \"AuthDigestQop none\" or the \"authdigest-opaque\"\n  Mutex type no longer start (the shipped manual still documents\n  \"AuthDigestQop none\"); RFC 2069 clients (no qop) are refused; no\n  Authentication-Info on 401/407; 503, or 401 without a challenge, if no\n  client entry fits in shared memory; log ids AH01767, AH01771, AH01772,\n  AH01792 and AH01793 are removed\n- mod_auth_digest: after a reload (graceful restart) a captured request is\n  accepted once more under AuthDigestNonceLifetime 0 or AuthDigestNcCheck;\n  only a full restart invalidates it (fixed upstream only in trunk\n  f4c4160fbf, not in 2.4.69)",
